From 8426dc0be03a469fdbc70bf61f71a32291590897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:40:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): G82/G89 dwell reopens the cycle on Fanuc, Mazak,
 Doosan, grblHAL and Tormach

The dwell is now part of the cycle signature for G82 and G89 (and G86 on
grblHAL and Tormach, which write a G86 P). A changed dwell writes G80 and
a new cycle block with its own P, as #2350 did for Haas. A back-bore with
no dwell posts G85 instead of a G89 with no P, so no modal P stays active
and no P word is required.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/dwell_cycles_modal_p.rs.

Fixes #2360

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
